---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../content/site.ts';
---

<Layout
  title={`Terms of Service — ${site.writer.name} Commissioned Fiction`}
  description="The full terms for commissioning Everayy: scope of work, payment and refund policy, revision rounds, cancellation, content rights, and how credit is handled."
>
  <main class="page">
    <a href="/" class="back-link" aria-label="Back to home">← Back</a>
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1 transition:name="page-title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Please read these terms carefully before commissioning work. By placing
        an order you agree to the following.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        I'm willing to write original works and characters, fanfiction and
        fandom-specific original characters, erotica and NSFW, character
        sheets/profiles/fan-wikis, as well as darker topics you might see
        classified under the "Dead Dove: Do Not Eat" umbrella.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fandoms I work with include: <strong>A Song of Ice and Fire</strong>,
        <strong>Fire &amp; Blood</strong>, <strong>A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms</strong>,
        <strong>House of the Dragon</strong>, <strong>Game of Thrones</strong>,
        <strong>Arcane: League of Legends</strong>, <strong>League of Legends</strong>,
        <strong>Neon Genesis Evangelion</strong>, <strong>True Detective</strong>,
        <strong>Chainsaw Man</strong>, <strong>Pirates of the Caribbean</strong>,
        and <strong>Star Trek: The Original Series</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also write fanfiction of any film in English or Brazilian Portuguese
        with subtitles available in at least one of these languages.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Payment</h2>
      <p>
        All prices are USD. Payment is made via Ko-fi — you can use either
        PayPal or Stripe. I take part of the payment upfront and part after the
        work is finished.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prices may vary depending on the complexity of the commission. I will
        never charge additional fees without your knowledge and explicit
        consent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Revisions</h2>
      <p>
        After the initial outline, I work on a weekly update basis. There is no
        fixed estimated time frame for me to deliver the complete work, but
        communication is always constant.
      </p>
      <p>
        You have the right to request up to three major free-of-charge changes
        during the writing process — that is, changes that impact the bulk of
        the work and require extensive rewrites.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Refunds &amp; Cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        I hold the right to reject any commission offer I'm not particularly
        comfortable with, though I'm open to much.
      </p>
      <p>
        Refunds are always allowed before the writing process has started, or
        if I'm unable to finish the commission for any reason. Completed works
        can't be refunded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Rights &amp; Credit</h2>
      <p>
        After the work is completed, it will be posted to AO3 and you'll be
        sent a file of the written work through your email. You can ask for as
        many copies as you want.
      </p>
      <p>
        I reserve the right to promote the commissioned work. You are free to
        share, print, and repost my work with the proper credit. I ask that you
        do not use my writing for profit nor claim ownership of it. I further
        ask that you do not feed my writing to AI learning models.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
